<title>HONG KONG: Yeebo posts HK$22.3 mln interim net loss.</title>
<headline>Yeebo posts HK$22.3 mln interim net loss.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   4.95 loss  vs 3.57 gain (see note)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	  vs 1.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  10.88 loss vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    22.32 loss vs 15.99 profit</p>
<p>    Turnover		     162.66     vs 175.32</p>
<p>    Company name		 Yeebo (International Holdings) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Yeebo (International Holdings) manufactures liquid crystal displays and printed circuit boards.</p>
<p>The company reported an operating loss of HK$13.28 million due to provision for diminution in value of a subsidiary and loss on sale of motor vehicles.</p>
<p>Exceptional loss represents loss on fixed assets no longer required for the group's operations.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
